title: The Central Committee Votes
subtitle: The party chooses its leaders for 1924.
new-page: true
tags: event
view-if: congress_reckoning = 2
max-visits: 1
priority: 9
on-arrival: {!
Q.e23_rk_old = Q.leading_faction;
RG.congressEnd();
var w = Q.congress_result;
var motion = {unionist: 'Brandler', offensive: 'the Left', luxemburgist: 'the middle group', ultraleft: 'the council communists'};
var cnt = ['unionist', 'offensive', 'luxemburgist', 'ultraleft'].filter(function (f) { return Q['congress_share_' + f] > 0; });
cnt.sort(function (a, b) { return Q['congress_share_' + b] - Q['congress_share_' + a]; });
Q.e23_rk_count = cnt.map(function (f, i) { return Q['congress_share_' + f] + (i == 0 ? ' per cent for ' : ' for ') + motion[f]; }).join(', ');
Q.e23_reckoning = {unionist: 1, offensive: 2, luxemburgist: 3}[w] || 5;
if (w == Q.e23_rk_old && w != 'unionist') { Q.e23_reckoning = 5; }
Q.lead_code = RG.CODE[Q.leading_faction] || 3;
Q.e23_rk_can_purge = (w == 'offensive' && Q.unionist_gone == 0) ? 1 : 0;
Q.e23_rk_kept = (Q.e23_reckoning == 5) ? 1 : 0;
Q.e23_rk_left_present = Q.offensive_gone == 0 ? 1 : 0;
if (w == 'unionist') {
    Q.unionist_satisfaction += 4;
    Q.offensive_satisfaction -= 8;
    Q.independence += 3;
    RG.ecci('zinoviev', -8);
    RG.ecci('radek', 4);
} else if (w == 'offensive') {
    RG.ecci('zinoviev', 8);
    RG.ecci('bukharin', 5);
    RG.ecci('radek', -6);
    RG.setRole('fischer', 'Chair of the Zentrale');
    RG.setRole('thalmann', 'Zentrale; chairman-designate');
} else if (w == 'luxemburgist') {
    RG.setRole('pieck', 'Zentrale; middle group');
    RG.ecci('zinoviev', -2);
}
RG.news('Central Committee: the ' + Q.congress_result_name + ' take the party into 1924', 3);
!}

= The Central Committee Votes

The vote is by show of hands, and it is counted twice because Maslow disputes the first count. The resolution of the **[+ congress_result_name +]** is carried with [+ e23_rk_count +]. [? if congress_close_call = 1 : Two hands go the other way on the second count, and that decides it. ?]

[? if e23_reckoning = 1 : Brandler keeps the Zentrale. He promises the united front, work in the unions and no more risings planned in Moscow. A telegram from Zinoviev arrives during the vote and is left unopened on the table. ?][? if e23_reckoning = 2 : The Left has the Central Committee. Ruth Fischer and Arkadi Maslow will run the Zentrale with Thälmann, and their first motion asks who exactly gave the order to stand down. ?][? if e23_reckoning = 3 : Pieck, Remmele and Eberlein take the Zentrale between them. Both camps have agreed to wait for the next congress. ?][? if e23_reckoning = 5 : The Zentrale stays as it was, and the resolution on 1923 is worded so that everyone can vote for it. ?]

- @brandler_moscow: Send Brandler and Thalheimer to Moscow.
- @purge: Expel Brandler's Right from the party.
- @middle_left: Give the Left its seats in the new Zentrale.
- @close: Close the session.

@brandler_moscow
subtitle: Moscow is pleased. The Right keeps its posts in Saxony and loses its leaders.
view-if: e23_rk_can_purge = 1
on-arrival: {!
RG.exile('brandler', {news: 'Brandler and Thalheimer summoned to Moscow'});
RG.exile('thalheimer', {quiet: true});
Q.unionist_satisfaction -= 10;
Q.independence -= 6;
RG.ecci('zinoviev', 4);
RG.ledger('The Central Committee gave the party to the Left; Brandler was sent to Moscow.', 'e23_reckoning');
!}

Brandler and Thalheimer are invited to Moscow for consultations, and given rooms at the Hotel Lux with no date of return.

@purge
subtitle: The Left governs alone. The Right's districts will go with their leaders.
view-if: e23_rk_can_purge = 1
on-arrival: {!
Q.e23_reckoning = 4;
RG.expel('brandler', {news: 'Brandler, Thalheimer and Walcher expelled'});
RG.expel('thalheimer', {quiet: true});
RG.expel('walcher', {quiet: true});
Q.unionist_gone = 1;
Q.unionist_satisfaction = 0;
Q.districts.forEach(function (d) {
    if (Q['district_' + d + '_faction'] == 'unionist') {
        Q['district_' + d + '_members'] *= 0.5;
        Q['district_' + d + '_faction'] = 'offensive';
        Q['district_' + d + '_loyalty'] = 50;
    }
});
if (Q.junior_faction == 'unionist') { Q.junior_faction = 0; }
Q.offensive_satisfaction += 10;
Q.unity += 5;
Q.worker_support -= 4;
Q.lean_offensive += 3;
RG.ledger('The Left expelled Brandler\'s Right at the end of 1923.', 'e23_reckoning');
!}

Brandler, Thalheimer and Walcher are expelled by a vote of the Central Committee. Half the Saxon membership leaves with them, and the old union men of Chemnitz start an opposition paper.

@middle_left
subtitle: The Left gets three seats, and the truce holds until the next congress.
view-if: e23_reckoning = 3 and e23_rk_left_present = 1
on-arrival: {!
Q.junior_faction = 'offensive';
Q.offensive_satisfaction += 6;
Q.unity += 4;
RG.ledger('A middle group took the Zentrale at the end of 1923, with the Left as junior partner.', 'e23_reckoning');
!}

Thälmann, Scholem and Fischer take their seats in the Zentrale on the understanding that nobody will be expelled before the congress.

@close
subtitle: The vote stands as it is.
on-arrival: {!
if (Q.e23_reckoning == 1) { RG.ledger('Brandler kept the Zentrale through the reckoning of December 1923.', 'e23_reckoning'); }
if (Q.e23_reckoning == 2) { RG.ledger('The Left took the Zentrale at the end of 1923.', 'e23_reckoning'); }
if (Q.e23_reckoning == 3) { RG.ledger('A middle group took the Zentrale at the end of 1923.', 'e23_reckoning'); }
Q.unity -= (Q.e23_reckoning == 5) ? 4 : 0;
!}

The Central Committee rises at four in the morning. [? if e23_reckoning = 2 : Brandler stays in Berlin without a post, and his friends write to Moscow. ?][? if e23_reckoning = 1 : The Left goes home to collect mandates for the next congress. ?][? if e23_reckoning = 3 : The Left goes home to collect mandates for the next congress. ?]
